# Export these variables before npm start; this file is not automatically loaded.
# Required: 32–4096 printable non-whitespace ASCII characters (bytes 0x21–0x7e).
# Generate a random secret; empty deliberately, never a production default.
# All authenticated clients act as this ONE operator, not separate users.
BASTION_TOKEN=
BASTION_OPERATOR_ID=local-admin
BASTION_PORT=8788
BASTION_DB=bastion.db
# Local alpha only: loopback HTTP, plaintext local SQLite journal, no shell execution.
# Unix DB and existing SQLite sidecars are restricted to 0600 at startup;
# new sidecars inherit the DB mode. Prefer launching with umask 077 as well.
# SIGINT/SIGTERM close HTTP, Socket.IO clients, and SQLite before exiting.
# D-013 checks trusted server time after BEGIN IMMEDIATE, not physical commit time.
# Wall clock must be synchronized externally. Invalid/backward observations fail closed;
# undetectable clock skew/forward jumps are not proof of trusted real-world time.
